[12.332566, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.369176, "o", "  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[N1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Sandbox network mode is VPC: network.mode is PUBLIC\r\n         fix: Set network.mode to VPC: no public network for model-written code.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[N2\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  No route to the internet: network.nat_gateway is true: the sandbox has a route out\r\n         fix: Remove the NAT gateway route from the sandbox subnets.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[N3\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Security group egress names its destinations: egress tcp/443 to 0.0.0.0/0\r\n         fix: Allow egress only to the endpoints and the proxy; no 0.0.0.0/0.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[N3\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Security group egress names its destinations: egress udp/53 to 0.0.0.0/0\r\n         fix: Allow egress only to the endpoints and the proxy; no 0.0.0.0/0.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[E1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Every endpoint has a custom endpoint policy: s3 gateway endpoint uses full-access\r\n         fix: Replace full-access with a policy that lists the actions and the resource ARNs this agent uses.\r\n"]
[12.369387, "o", "  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[E1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Every endpoint has a custom endpoint policy: bedrock-runtime interface endpoint uses full-access\r\n         fix: Replace full-access with a policy that lists the actions and the resource ARNs this agent uses.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[D1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  DNS resolver allow-list (walled garden) is on: dns.firewall is false: the resolver answers for any name\r\n         fix: Turn on the DNS firewall, block everything by default and allow only the names this agent needs.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[D2\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  DNS firewall fails closed: dns.fail_open is true\r\n         fix: Set dns.fail_open to false (the AWS default is fail closed).\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[L1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Every outbound door has a log: flow_logs off\r\n         fix: Turn on VPC flow logs, Resolver query logs and CloudTrail network activity events for each endpoint's service.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[L1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Every outbound door has a log: dns_query_logs off\r\n         fix: Turn on VPC flow logs, Resolver query logs and CloudTrail network activity events for each endpoint's service.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[L1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Every outbound door has a log: no CloudTrail network activity events for bedrock.amazonaws.com, s3.amazonaws.com\r\n         fix: Turn on VPC flow logs, Resolver query logs and CloudTrail network activity events for each endpoint's service.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[P1\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Proxy allow-list names exact hosts: proxy allows *.amazonaws.com\r\n         fix: Replace wildcard entries with the exact host names.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[P2\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  The proxy is enforced by the network: proxy.enforced_by_network is false: code that ignores the proxy goes straight out\r\n         fix: Make the proxy the only address the sandbox can reach on the web ports (security group), not just an env var.\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[P3\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Proxy allows only the methods each host needs: proxy allows every method to *.amazonaws.com\r\n         fix: List methods per host (GET and HEAD for a package mirror).\r\n  \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K[P3\u001b[m\u001b[K] 27.2  Proxy allows only the methods each host needs: proxy allows every method to pypi.tsg.example\r\n         fix: List methods per host (GET and HEAD for a package mirror).\r\n"]
